# Chat stays in chat

Copyright (c) 2026 Devrecated.

Never copy a chat instruction, aside, or “keep this quiet” note into a repo file.

That includes LICENSE, NOTICE, README, legal/IP docs, employee guides, Project readmes, mail HTML, commits, and comments.

Chat-only (do **not** write these into files):

- “Do not email this file”
- “Don’t tell the client / stakeholders”
- “Keep this secret / between us”
- “This would be embarrassing if they saw it”
- Process asides meant only for the agent in this thread

```md
<!-- BAD — chat aside leaked into LICENSE.md -->
**Do not email this file.** Stakeholder mail must never mention copyright.

<!-- GOOD — LICENSE states ownership only -->
This repository contains two ownership classes.
```

Agent process belongs in `.cursor/rules/` or a skill, not in LICENSE or client-facing docs. If the user said something is secret or not to be included, leave it out of the tree. When unsure, ask — do not paste it “just in case.”
